  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment (config_001, rna_only/pca_n2000/singleprofile) has been completed, yielding a low accuracy of 0.485 and F1 of 0.464, indicating the task is challenging and the current RNA representation captures limited signal. Uncertainty: The most fundamental unknown is whether the image modality carries useful discriminative signal for this task. Without knowing this, it is impossible to prioritize among the many multimodal configurations or to decide whether to invest in better RNA encoders. What this tests: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_001, isolating the effect of modality while holding profile_setting constant. Why it is the best use of the next budget: If image accuracy substantially exceeds 0.485, it justifies prioritizing multimodal configurations and stronger image encoders (ViT-L). If it is comparable or lower, it confirms RNA is the stronger (or equally weak) modality and shifts focus to better RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt) or multiprofile aggregation. Either outcome dramatically narrows the search space for all subsequent experiments, making this the highest-information experiment available."
}

